This YANI proposes a "prepolymorph" option.  When this is set to the name of a
monster, the hero begins polymorphed into that monster or a juvenile version of
it, wearing an amulet of unchanging, and the underlying role monster is
genocided.  (Perhaps a horrible incident up on the surface, which our hero
escaped only by being polyed at the time.  S/he now hopes to reverse this mess
by finding the Amulet and delivering it to his/her god.)  Starting wielded
weapons or armor that the polyed form cannot use will not be generated.

The self-poly logic is *not* altered, except for the "growing up" feature
described below.  Removing that amulet will lead to YASD if you happen to
revert.  Perhaps it could start off cursed.  Watch out for nymphs!  Also, you
heal at the monster rate, not the human rate.

The monster must of course be one to which self-poly is permitted.  No, you
can't play as an Archon.  Also, if a monster has "grown-up" forms, the lowest
form is chosen:  if you say "arch-lich" then you'll start off as a plain lich. 
As you gain experience, you'll advance to the next higher form -- unless it's
genocided, in which case you go poof.  YASD.  Some additional polymorphs may
have to be restricted -- an Aleax player could unbalance the game.

Some immediate observations:
* A lawful or neutral polyed into a demon is unable to pray.  A lawful polyed
into an undead will be reverted if he prays; a neutral runs a one in ten chance
of meeting this fate.
* Further self-polymorph is effectively permanent.  Uncontrolled polymorph
carries a risk of YASD.  Of course, the amulet of unchanging will prevent it
from happening, but there's the further risk arising from not being able to
spring poly traps.



